// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`documents history deletion boundaries in offline help 1`] = `
"Usage: opencove agent history clear --node <id> [options]

Delete a node’s stored OpenCove replies without deleting the node

Deletes this node’s stored ended-turn replies from the Worker archive and in-memory history across all retained incarnations. Does not delete the node, provider transcripts or backups, and does not change run state, active turns or delivery records. A turn that ends after the clear is stored normally.

Returns nodeId, memoryRemoved and archive: {status: cleared, removed}. Counts are per store; the same reply may have a copy in each. Repeating the command succeeds with zero counts. Requires interact scope. If the archive is unavailable, memory is still cleared; exits 1 with archive: {status: unavailable} and memoryRemoved in the error details, without claiming archive deletion. For an agent on a remote Worker it clears only local copies and exits 1 with details.reason: remote_history_unavailable.

Options:
  --node <id>         Select a canvas node by its ID; also accepts @self, @parent, an exact name or a unique ID prefix (6+ characters) (required)
  --space <selector>  Require every node selector, including full IDs, to belong to this space; also accepts @self, an exact name or a unique ID prefix (6+ characters)
  --project <id>      Narrow target lookup to a project; also accepts @self, an exact name or a unique ID prefix (6+ characters)

Table output (-o table): not supported.
Projectable fields: nodeId, memoryRemoved, archive, archive.status, archive.removed

Projection example:
  opencove agent history clear --node '<id>' --fields nodeId
  {"nodeId":"node-123","memoryRemoved":2,"archive":{"status":"cleared","removed":3}}

Examples:
  opencove agent history clear --node "Reviewer"

Global options: see "opencove --help".
"
`;
